{{also|þu|-þu}}
==Icelandic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|is|-du|-ðu|-u}} {{q|enclitic forms}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|þú}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*þū}}, from {{inh|is|ine-pro|*túh₂}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|thou}}, {{cog|de|du}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/θu/|[θuː]}}
* {{audio|is|Is-Þú.oga|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|is|uː|s=1}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun|cat2=personal pronouns}}

# {{lb|is|personal|singular}} [[you]], [[thou]]
#: {{ux|is|'''Þú''' [[vera#Icelandic|ert]] [[skemmtilegur]].|'''You''' [[are]] [[fun]].}}
#: {{ux|is|Er'''tu''' nemandi?|Are '''you''' a student?}}

====Usage notes====
After verbs, the pronoun {{m|is|þú}} is either separated: 
* {{uxi|is|ert '''þú'''|are '''you'''}}
* {{uxi|is|borðar '''þú'''|do '''you''' eat}}
* {{uxi|is|kom '''þú'''|come!}}
or suffixed and changed into {{m|is|-ðu}}, {{m|is|-du}}, or {{m|is|-u}}:
* {{uxi|is|ert'''u'''|are '''you'''}}
* {{uxi|is|borðar'''ðu'''|do '''you''' eat}}
* {{uxi|is|kom'''du'''|come!}}

If the verb ends in a "t", {{m|is|-u}} is used. If it ends in a "m" or "n", {{m|is|-du}} is used. Otherwise {{m|is|-ðu}} is used.

The suffixed version is almost always used except when the speaker wants to emphasize "þú" or sound more formal.

Many younger speakers will write {{m|is||borðar'''u'''}} instead of {{m|is||borðar'''ðu'''}} as that is how the word is pronounced

